	abstract = {Research on the visual processing of advertisements has so far focused on formal aspects such as the relative size of print or the composition of graphical elements. Little is known, however, about effects of specific content-related design factors. One such factor is the complexity of the pragmatic relation between image and text. We refer to an advertisement as “explicit” when it depicts the target product (e.g. a stereo or a car) together with a related headline in a semantically straightforward way. In contrast, an “implicit” advertisement includes pictures and text neither of which are directly related to the product.},
